@startuml 30_cloud_deployment
title FleetLuma - final cloud topology with v0.1.0 pairing (DESIGN TARGET)
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
node "Authorized operators" {
 component "Flutter Web (Vercel static)" as Web
 component "Flutter Android" as Android
}
node "Windows monitored host" {
 artifact "Agent setup UI (Flutter desktop)" as WindowsUI
 component "Python psutil Windows service" as WindowsAgent
}
node "Ubuntu/Debian monitored host" {
 artifact "Agent setup UI (Flutter Linux / CLI headless)" as LinuxUI
 component "Python psutil systemd daemon" as LinuxAgent
}
cloud "Vercel FleetLuma team" {
 component "FastAPI Python Functions\nEnrollment + reporting + device management" as API
}
node "Supabase FleetLuma" {
 database "PostgreSQL private fleetluma schema\nworkspaces, memberships, pairings, hosts, samples, audit" as PG
 component "Supabase Auth\noperator JWT issuer" as Auth
 component "Scheduled HTTP checker\nEdge Function / Cron (FL-19)" as Scheduler
}
cloud "Allowlisted public HTTP endpoints" as Endpoints
WindowsUI --> WindowsAgent : protected local named pipe
LinuxUI --> LinuxAgent : restricted UNIX socket
WindowsAgent --> API : HTTPS pairing and reporting
LinuxAgent --> API : HTTPS pairing and reporting
Web --> API : HTTPS approved JWT, scoped fleet + device approval
Android --> API : HTTPS approved JWT, scoped fleet + device approval
Web --> Auth : operator login
Android --> Auth : operator login
API --> Auth : validate JWKS, issuer, audience
API --> PG : pooled private TLS SQL transactions
Scheduler --> Endpoints : approved bounded HTTP probes
Scheduler --> PG : checks and retention
note bottom of API
 No SQLite in cloud, no background scheduler
 No Vercel SSO challenge at agent API (machine traffic)
 Pairing code display-only; reporting secret stays on agent
end note
note bottom of PG
 Additive migration preserves existing TUFFEST and samples.
 No direct browser/database exposure.
end note
@enduml
